        "protected": 12.0,
        "manageable": 30.0
      }
    },
    "negative_ihc_rule": "Relax only with valid Not detected observations in every routine IHC tissue/cell context mapping to the same anatomical tissue as the RNA measurement. Use the weakest reliability among all observations in that tissue. Missing contexts, unknown reliability, invalid observations, positive staining or reviewed-unreliable IHC cannot earn relaxation. A narrower region cannot clear a broader organ; other organs cannot supply negative evidence. Enhanced describes source validation, not a guaranteed limit of detection for a negative stain or for peptide-HLA presentation.",
    "negative_ihc_minimum_reproductive_selectivity": {
      "Missing": {
        "vital": 0.75,
        "protected": 0.7,
        "manageable": 0.65
      },
      "Uncertain": {
        "vital": 0.75,
        "protected": 0.7,
        "manageable": 0.65
      },
      "Approved": {
        "vital": 0.7,
        "protected": 0.65,
        "manageable": 0.6
      },
      "Supported": {
        "vital": 0.65,
        "protected": 0.6,
        "manageable": 0.55
      },
      "Enhanced": {
        "vital": 0.6,
        "protected": 0.55,
        "manageable": 0.5
      }
    },
    "reproductive_selectivity": {
      "formula": "Rmax / (Rmax + tissue_rna_ntpm)",
      "reference": "Maximum valid raw RNA across mapped Reproductive tissues for the same gene, species, source and version. Disposable does not enter the reference.",
      "minimum_reference": "Strictly positive; a zero or missing reference is unresolved.",
      "comparison": "Inclusive minimum per screened RNA observation. The same local negative-IHC evidence chooses both the RNA ceiling and selectivity threshold.",
      "aggregation": "Every screened tissue must pass both gates. Category summaries report the worst margin against its own threshold, not a pooled category score.",
      "meaning": "Pairwise expression selectivity, not percent of total-body RNA or protein. Uses raw nTPM without deflation, averaging, tissue sums or rounding before gating.",
      "provenance": "User-approved target-informed project recalibration on 2026-10-21. The previous percentage ladder was too stringent when transferred from a global deflated fraction to a raw pairwise score. The new grid preserves higher protection for Vital and relaxes with local negative-IHC confidence. Named CTA recovery is a calibration check, not independent validation."
    },
    "threshold_provenance": "Vital absolute limits remain 1/2/3/6 nTPM and Manageable remains 5/10/15/30. Protected changes to 3/4/6/12, including a general baseline increase from 2 to 3 that admits the pinned CT83 salivary value of 2.6. Selectivity minima are Vital 75/70/65/60%, Protected 70/65/60/55%, and Manageable 65/60/55/50% for Missing-or-Uncertain/Approved/Supported/Enhanced. These are user-approved research parameters under the requested recalibration, not clinically validated values or limits estimated from patient outcomes. Both gates and the positive-IHC veto apply to every screened tissue. Literature supports graded priorities, not these exact values or a GTEx-to-HPA conversion. HPA reliability labels are evidence strata, not probabilities of negative staining or peptide-HLA absence."
  },
